  "directive_events": [
    {
      "at": "2026-08-07T00:49:28.764975Z",
      "owner_directive": "Capture the decisions from the live discussion into the spec before continuing",
      "reason": "plan"
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-08-07T02:11:33.653857Z",
      "owner_directive": "Users may have no codebase at all \u2014 pure spreadsheet or GUI-software workflows. Add an 'I have no codebase' option to the source choice, make the workflow-description question required in that mode, and generalise the whole feature so people who do not process data with code can use it. Name the entry 'Bring in my work'.",
      "reason": "Owner generalised the feature to users with no codebase and renamed it"
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-08-07T02:35:37.801296Z",
      "owner_directive": "Verification is over-specified. Keep it flexible: if the codebase has data, the agent tells the user it will verify with it; if not, it asks whether the user can supply some; with no codebase it asks the same. Also, a MATLAB codebase should be transcribed to Python rather than declared out of scope \u2014 say 'other languages' without enumerating them.",
      "reason": "Owner simplified verification to a flexible agent-led flow and put cross-language transcription in scope"
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-08-07T02:46:08.364481Z",
      "owner_directive": "The task instructions must not flood the user's terminal. Since most providers are AMBIENT and cannot take a hidden per-session prompt, unify: after the dialog is answered, write the assembled brief to a hidden location under .scistudio/, and let the only visible message be one line saying the task is described at that path, for the agent to read itself.",
      "reason": "Owner chose file-based brief delivery so behaviour is uniform across providers and the terminal is not flooded"
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-08-07T03:18:56.998149Z",
      "owner_directive": "The brief opens by telling the agent it is helping the user migrate a body of work and outlines the workflow, then the checklist, then the delivery standard, then the working method, then the user's answers. Delivery: types for the user's common data kinds with IO blocks for formats core lacks; blocks decomposing one or two workflows with at least one interactive block; app blocks for named software; one block per step with user-facing metadata; a demo workflow (optional); at least one previewer with interaction designed for the data. Before implementing, the agent presents its plan in the user's own terms - your data kind becomes a type, your steps become blocks, this step can pause for you, this needs a viewer - then asks for the user's view.",
      "reason": "Owner specified the brief's structure, delivery standard, and working method"
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-08-07T04:11:10.320139Z",
      "owner_directive": "We only handled the case where no provider is available. If the user has several usable providers we never let them choose. Add provider selection and the permission choice to the dialog's first page, below the source and destination fields, matching what the AI chat setup screen in PR #2003 offers.",
      "reason": "Owner spotted that multiple usable providers were unhandled; dialog gains provider and permission controls"
    }
  ],
